<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14482" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">distractor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id. I.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One who worries</i>, <i>a
			tormenter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">improbus (i. e. Achilles),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Anthol. Lat. 1, 93, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A retailer</i>, Cod. Th. 11, 1, 4: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argenti,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a money-changer</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Just. 8, 14, 27</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">12, 35 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
